:: Adulthood [Adult] {"position":"600,1150","size":"100,100"}
You awake on a cool, winter Saturday in your <<do>> <<if $married>> own 2-story home <<else>> apartment<</if>><</do>>.

 <<do>> <<if $married>>Your partner's left for the day, and you have the house you yourself.<<else>>It's quiet living alone. You never did get that cat you considered a few years back. Oh well.<</if>><</do>>. 
 
You head to the kitchen to make toast and coffee, and open the morning paper on your phone. As you sit at the table to eat, you get an Instagram notification.

Aria, your friend from high school, reached out to you.

//"Hey! Long time, no see :) Want to grab coffee and catch up?"//

[[Why not? I've got the whole day ahead of me|Coffee with Aria]]


:: Aria Goodbye [Adult mini-scene] {"position":"1100,1250","size":"100,100"}

<<do>>
	<<if $aria == "teach"|| $aria == "advance">>
    	"That's noble of you. From what I know, and from what you've told me, I'm sure you'll do just that."
    <<else>>
    	"Well...there's always time to try to change that..."
    <</if>>
<</do>>

With this, she stands to leave, gathering her things while you collect your cups to put in the <<do>><<if $sustainabilityScore >= 5>>recycling <<else>> trash<</if>><</do>>. 

"I have a flight to catch," she says, "But I'm really<<do>><<if $aria == "teach"|| $aria == "advance">> so glad <<else>>... glad <</if>><</do>>we did this."

[[Garden Check 3]] 


:: Ask Dad [mini-scene] {"position":"1550,775","size":"100,100"}
You walk downstairs, and grab your grandmother's sewing kit from the kitchen drawer.

You approach your father on the couch, and ask him if he could sew the button back on your shirt. 


He smiles at you and pats the spot next to him on the couch, inviting you to sit with him.

"Whatever you choose to do, I know you'll be spectacular. You're smart, thoughtful, and kind, and we're all so //so// proud of you."

He ties off the knot on the inside of your shirt, and pushes off your shoulder to stand up. 

You stand in front of him and put on your newly-mended shirt. You're a whole head taller than him now, but you let him button your last few buttons and adjust your collar. He's feeling sentimental.

"Sharp as ever," he beams. "Ready to go?"

[[Go to graduation|Graduation]]


:: At school [School-Age] {"position":"925,650","size":"100,100"}
You arrive at school, greeting your teacher and friends as students trickle in. After a few moments, as the class settles, your teacher starts today’s lesson 

“Good morning, class! Today, we’re going to continue our discussion of Zombies in 21st-century Films. Who can tell me a tenet of this genre and how it could relate to sustainability?”


[["Zombie movies usually treat the apocalypse at the result of an major disease outbreak that was mishandled by governments and public health organizations and for which society as unprepared."|Lecture Continues][$teacherPraise to "Exactly!"; $sustainabilityScore to  $sustainabilityScore + 5]]

[["People usually have to quarantine to protect themselves from the virus. That's part of public health and sustainability."|Lecture Continues][$teacherPraise to "That's a start!"; $sustainabilityScore to  $sustainabilityScore + 1]]

[["Don’t raise your hand"|Lecture Continues][ $teacherPraise to "I guess I'll fill in some gaps."; $sustainabilityScore to  $sustainabilityScore - 1]]




:: Borrow [mini-scene] {"position":"1450,775","size":"100,100"}
You race downstairs and out the front door, yelling "I love you!" to your grandmother grabbing a biscuit for Sam on the way.

You tear down the street and trip up the front steps of the Wilkins' house. You compose yourself to calmly–//respectfully//–knock on the front door.

Sam answers, late as ever, but this time almost entirely dressed. You thrust the biscuit into his chest

"Sam! I need–" you cough, winded "–a shirt. My button–"

"Yeah, yeah! I've got one. Come on."

He waves you in, already halfway through the biscuit by the time you both find clean, fitting shirts.

"Ready to go?" he asks.

[[Go to graduation|Graduation]]


:: Childhood - Start Here [School-Age] {"position":"600,500","size":"100,100"}
You wake up in a simple two-story family ranch home to your grandmother calling you downstairs. She’s made you breakfast before school, tofu scramble, fish and rice, and fresh biscuits.

//What would you like to eat?//

<<linkreplace "Hmm... tofu and a biscuit">>Eat up! A full belly is a fueled brain<</linkreplace>>
<<linkreplace "Oooh, Fish and Rice">>Eat up! A full belly is a fueled brain<</linkreplace>>
<<linkreplace "Just a biscuit, please">>I do wish you'd eat more. Breakfast is the most important meal of the day<</linkreplace>>



<<link [[Finish Eating|finish eating]]>><</link>>


:: Coffee with Aria [Adult] {"position":"800,1150","size":"100,100"}
In the afternoon, you head to the coffee shop. You remove your hat and coat as you walk in an scan the crowd for Aria.

You see her waving from a small wooden table near the back corner of the shop.

She greets you warmly, and you both sit. After you both order and have settled with your respective beverages. 

"Gosh, 20 years," she exclaims. "What are you doing these days?"

<<do>>
	<<if $college>>
    	<<if $major == "art">>
    	[[I'm an urban designer, an eco-designed specifically. I focus on walkable and sustainable city development|Hobbies?][$sustainabilityScore += 3]]
        <<else>>
        [[I went into public health research. I've helped with a couple prevention inititatives and helped reduce cost for local clinics.|Hobbies?][$sustainabilityScore += 3]]
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $work>>
    [[I'm a manager at the $power plant now.|Hobbies?]]
    <<else>>
		[[Keeping busy, mostly, staying connected with my community. You know, events organizing, mutual aid, odd jobs in the neighborhood. Helping my fellow man and what not|Hobbies?][$sustainabilityScore += 1]]
    <</if>>
<</do>>


:: College or Career [Young-Adult] {"position":"1100,925","size":"100,100"}
You head downstairs, where your mother is cooking breakfast, while your father and sibling play gin rummy on the couch. Over the sizzle of the stove, you hear your mother ask:

"Are you still thinking about college? Of course, you don't have to work, but if you still want to keep busy, it could be a good option"


[[I think college is the right choice for me|Mom Reply][$college = true; $momReply to "I remember you said you talked to Jannah about a some ideas about your major at graduation. You better get your applications in soon"]]
[[No, I'm still weighing the pros and cons|Mom Reply][$momReply to "What have you thought of so far? I know you said you wanted to keep busy as an adult, but you know you don't have to do either if you don't want to."]]
[[Actually, I think working could be good for me. Something small |Mom Reply][$momReply to "What have you thought of so far? I know you said you wanted to keep busy as an adult, but you know you don't have to do either if you don't want to.";$work = true]]
 


:: DIY [mini-scene] {"position":"1350,775","size":"100,100"}

You find your grandmother's sewing kit in a kitchen drawer and sit at the table.

You sew the button back onto your shirt, while your grandmother offers some sage advice.

"Do you know why I taught you to sew when you were little?"

"No," you reply, "why?"

"Every time you patch a hole or hem a pant leg or sew a button, you have to sit a while... I did it so I could spend more time with you"

You smile at her while you tie of the knot on the inside of your shirt. You kiss her cheek while you button your shirt, and suddenly, you're ready to go.

[[Go to graduation|Graduation]]


