:: Get Ready for Graduation [School-Age] {"position":"1450,650","size":"100,100"}
...it is the morning of your high school graduation. You are serving your grandmother breakfast, while your sibling does the dishes from a rickety wooden step-stool. As you sit to eat, your mother comes down the stairs. 

She rests a hand on your shoulder and smiles at you warmly. “This day came so much sooner than we could’ve imagined. I’m so proud of you”

She bends down to kiss your forehead, when your father notices the time.

“Eat fast, you don’t want to be late!”

You check the stove clock and wolf down the rest of your breakfast. You race upstairs, and as you are rushing to get dressed, a button pops off the front of your shirt.

//You have to fix this wardrobe malfunction! Fast!//

[[Borrow a shirt from Mrs. Wilkins|Borrow][$sustainabilityScore += 5]]
[[Ask your father to repair it|Ask Dad][$sustainabilityScore += 3]]
[[Repair it yourself|DIY][$sustainabilityScore += 1]]


:: Go get dressed [School-Age] {"position":"750,650","size":"100,100"}
You kiss your grandmother goodbye, hand your sibling a biscuit, and grab your bag. 

Your father stops you on the way out.

“Your mother and Mrs. Wilkins went to work early this morning. Could you drop off food at the Wilkins’ and walk Sam to school?

What will you do with the food?

<<link [[Take the food, save it for lunch at school|Lunch]]>><</link>>
<<link [[Take the food, leave it at the door|Leave at Door]]>><</link>>
<<link [[Take the food, and wait for Sam to eat so you can walk to school together|Walk with Sam]]>><</link>>


:: Graduation [School-Age Transition] {"position":"1700,650","size":"100,100"}
Your principal takes the stage to address you and your classmates.

“Students, you have spent years nurturing your creativity, developing your morals and ethics, and critically examining the world around you, and now you prepare to embark into adulthood, hopefully prepared and unabashedly excited. We hope that we have endowed you with the tools to make the changes //you// want to see in the world. ''Congratulations to the graduating class of 2126!''”

As the excitement dims to a gentle thrum among the crowd, your friend Jannah turns to hug you, celebrating your mutual achievement. Jannah asks, “So what changes do you want to see in the world?”


[["I like creating. I think I have important things to say"|Garden Check 1][$sustainabilityScore +=1;$major = "art"]]
[["I want to help with public health and medicine."|Garden Check 1][$sustainabilityScore +=3;$major = "public health"]]
[["I don’t know yet, but I'm excited to find out"|Garden Check 1]]


:: Hobbies? [Adult] {"position":"950,1150","size":"100,100"}
<<do>>
  <<if $work>>
      <<if $power == "solar">>
          "That sounds so much like you. And you seem happy. Personally, I've been..."
          <<set $sustainabilityScore += 4>>
      <<else>>
          <<set $sustainabilityScore -= 4>>
          "That's...unusual. And not all that good for the environment. Personally, I've been..."
      <</if>>
  <<else>>
  	"That sounds so much like you. And you seem happy. Personally, I've been..."
  <</if>>
<</do>>

She talks for a few minutes about the traveling she's been doing with a few NGOs and non-profits. Namibia with Doctors without Borders. Puerto Rico with Habitat for Humanity. After a moment, she pauses

"I'm sorry. I don't mean to ramble, it's just been a while since I've had anyone to tell about it. I gave up travel influencing a few years ago."

Vaguely, you recall a few videos on your feed of Aria's Christmas in Dubai a couple years back. You wave her off, enjoying the conversation regardless

"What else do you do?" she asks, "Where are you living?"

[[I inherited my parents' house after they passed, so I spend a lot of time just thinking about when we were kids. Trying to make sure the world stays that way for other generations. |Legacy][$sustainabilityScore += 1]]
[[I actually live in communal housing, so I spend a lot of time with my co-habitants. Last week, I helped Sarah's son with his science fair project. I think he's really going to be something grea |Legacy][$sustainabilityScore += 3]]




:: Leave at Door [mini-scene] {"position":"600,775","size":"100,100"}
You take the food from your father and head down the street to the Wilkins' house. You set the bag gently on the front steps and ring the doorbell. 

You hear footsteps coming toward the door, and decide that since the food is delivered, you don't want to wait for Sam to eat. You already brought him food, you've done enough

<<set $sustainabilityScore to $sustainabilityScore  - 2>>

[[Head to school->At school]]


:: Lecture Continues [School-Age] {"position":"1125,650","size":"100,100"}
“$teacherPraise Horror and sci-fi are often used as a speculative genre to predict and explore how humanity may respond to or change due to different events. In the case of zombie movies, the event is a public health crisis or a pandemic. We’ve watched several here in class and talked plenty. How about some questions to get us thinking from a different angle!”

 [[“Why weren’t zombie movies less popular after the 2020 COVID pandemic? They seem like they’d be more boring than the real thing”|Question 1][$teacherPraise to "A very good question. Go read a few articles about the pandemic in the library and compare them to movie reviews from the '20s. Tell me what you think tomorrow"; $destination to "library";$sustainabilityScore += 3]]

[[“Have we improved our public health response? Has it made us more sustainable?”|Question 2][$teacherPraise to "It depends on who you ask! Do some research on public health metrics and opinions. Compare how things have changed. You might find an interesting answer"; $destination to "library";$sustainabilityScore +=1]]

[[“Can I use the restroom?”|Question 3][$teacherPraise to "You may.";$destination to "bathroom";$sustainabilityScore -=2]]




:: Legacy [Adult] {"position":"1100,1150","size":"100,100"}
"It sounds like you've really made a life for yourself then. Fulfilled and happy, and surprisingly optimistic. Do you have any hopes for those future generations? Anything you think you'll pass on?"

<<do>>
<<if $sustainabilityScore >= 8>>
  [[I want to pass on my knowledge to younger generations on how to improve our sustainable world.|Aria Goodbye][$aria to "teach"]]

  [[I want to push for more changes and technological advances to keep improving our society. |Aria Goodbye][$aria to "advance"]]
  <<else>>
  [[At this point, I'm not sure there's much of anything to pass on|Aria Goodbye][$aria to "sad"]]
  <</if>>
<</do>>


